From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 03:15:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: describe the scaler and its
 DART

Add the MSR scaler/CSC engine and its DART from the J604 runtime ADT
(/arm-io/scaler0, /arm-io/dart-scaler):

  scaler0      0x505000000 +0x38000, 0x505210000 +0x4000,
               0x505204000 +0x4000, 0x504000000 +0x8000
               irq 1040 (MSR) and 1042 (PIODMA)
               hardware-version 0x14
               iommu-parent mapper-scaler (sid 0), mapper-scaler-piodma (sid 1)
  dart-scaler  0x505260000 +0x20000, irq 1041, sids 0 and 1,
               vm-base 0x10000000000, vm-size 0x30000000000

The ADT power gates are MSR-V (a virtual child of MSR, PMGR +0x560),
MSR_ASE_CORE (+0x568, child of MSR) and two MSR-SOC-VMAX/VNOM
performance votes; the two power states are ps_msr and ps_msr_ase_core,
and function-device_reset names state 0x99, MSR, so the engine reset is
ps_msr. The DART has no power gate of its own and sits in the MSR domain,
as on the T6040, where Aurora's J616s runs this driver with the same
DART window.

Every node is "disabled" here and ps_msr / ps_msr_ase_core stay
disabled in the board PMGR files, so nothing probes and no power state
changes until a board opts in.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 0d5fb8f364db71485440c9d8642a608298ac29b6)
(cherry picked from commit 6e4dfeda4cb25a97bb9c3d0e749f7ef1cd59524d)
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
index 666d8c5ac0..ca3223373d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
@@ -778,6 +778,38 @@
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * Scaler/CSC engine (MSR): J604 runtime ADT scaler0
+		 * (hardware-version 0x14) and dart-scaler (sids 0 and 1,
+		 * vm-base 0x10000000000, vm-size 0x30000000000). Power MSR and
+		 * MSR_ASE_CORE; the ADT device reset is the MSR state.
+		 */
+		scaler0: scaler@505000000 {
+			compatible = "apple,t8132-scaler", "apple,scaler";
+			reg = <0x5 0x05000000 0x0 0x38000>,
+			      <0x5 0x05210000 0x0 0x4000>,
+			      <0x5 0x05204000 0x0 0x4000>,
+			      <0x5 0x04000000 0x0 0x8000>;
+			interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
+			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 1040 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+				     <AIC_IRQ 1042 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			power-domains = <&ps_msr>, <&ps_msr_ase_core>;
+			resets = <&ps_msr>;
+			iommus = <&scaler0_dart 0>, <&scaler0_dart 1>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
+		scaler0_dart: iommu@505260000 {
+			compatible = "apple,t8132-dart", "apple,t8110-dart";
+			reg = <0x5 0x05260000 0x0 0x20000>;
+			interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
+			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 1041 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			#iommu-cells = <1>;
+			apple,dma-range = <0x100 0x0 0x300 0x0>;
+			power-domains = <&ps_msr>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		/*
 		 * The SEP DART's input aperture is the BIT(40) alias the DART
 		 * translates (ADT vm-base-0 0x10000004000).
-- 
2.43.0

